{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773532613,"nonce":"Vag1ijjLtPxTK2tXyICaGOHtCAQ=","title":"nightshift uses full session hash for git-bug commands, should use short ID","message":"## Problem\n\nAfter accepting/rejecting an issue, nightshift calls git-bug with the full 64-char issue hash from state.json:\n\n```\ngit-bug bug status close ddabba1413cc6b8e1b3e2bb2308e5e5b8e8e994b6c7b7bb8e29b879dc5f6bfb9\nError: you must provide a bug id or use the \"select\" command first\n```\n\ngit-bug only accepts short prefix IDs (7-12 chars), not full hashes. So post-merge cleanup (close issue, post comment) fails silently.\n\n## Root cause\n\nstate.json stores the full git-bug hash as issue_id. cli.py passes a.issue_id (user input) directly to tracker.set_status() and tracker.add_comment(). When the user types a short ID, it works. But the watcher and other automated paths pass the full hash from state.json.\n\n## Fix\n\nTruncate issue_id to SHORT_ID_LEN before passing to git-bug commands. Either:\n- In GitBugTracker methods (set_status, add_comment, etc.) — truncate at the adapter level\n- In cli.py before calling tracker methods — truncate at the call site\n\nAdapter level is better — git-bug always wants short IDs regardless of caller.\n\n## Requirement\n\nREQ-002 (Session lifecycle management)","files":null}]}